Folio OCR-only static TrueType fonts

The FolioOcrArabic, FolioOcrDevanagari, FolioOcrCjkSC, FolioOcrCjkJP and
FolioOcrCjkKR families are derived static regular instances of the Noto Sans
fonts from google/fonts revision 9862abc066c9b83bf84c3e8ed1fc2d8d48f9bbf0.
They are licensed under SIL OFL 1.1, not Apache-2.0. The full original
copyright notices and licenses are in ../NotoSans*.ttf.OFL.txt and are retained
in the generated third-party notices. The CJK upstream license reserves the
name "Source"; the derived fonts use new FolioOcr names instead.

Source URLs, upstream Git blob identities, upstream SHA-256 checksums and
derived file SHA-256 checksums are recorded in ../catalog.json. The existing
NotoSans-Regular.ttf is reused unchanged for Latin, Greek and Cyrillic.

Reproduction: scripts/instantiate-ocr-fonts.py --source <pinned-upstream-dir>
using fonttools 4.62.1. Every source is SHA-256 checked before instancing.
All weight axes are pinned at 400 and other axes at their defaults. Family,
style, unique and PostScript names are renamed; upstream timestamps, glyphs,
copyright and license tables are retained. No CFF program is declared as
FontFile2 and no variable font is embedded.

These fonts only supply real CID glyph references and metrics for invisible
logical OCR text. A word-sized CID maps to its full, exact UTF-16 Unicode
sequence, including combining marks and joiners. Exact recognized separators
have separate zero-advance Unicode CIDs mapped to the real space glyph;
they do not distort word selection boxes. Each span also carries the same
logical ActualText. Tr=3 ensures none of
these unshaped glyph references can replace or alter original scan pixels.
This is not general visible Arabic/Indic shaping or paragraph editing.
